{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>You have killed the people of HaShem</b> – Onkelos rendered (Onkelos on Numbers 17:6): \"You caused the death of the people of HaShem.\" He interprets it as holding them accountable for having given this counsel to offer unauthorized incense before HaShem, knowing that those who offered it would be consumed by fire, for HaShem did not say to Moses to offer this incense, and he did not tell Israel in the name of HaShem to do so. If so, of their own accord they gave this counsel by which the people died, when they could have provided some other sign or wonder with the staff or otherwise. And Ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 17:6): What proof is this that the tribe of Levi was chosen and Aaron was chosen as High Priest? It is possible that through your prayer or through wisdom that you knew, you burned those who offered. And so it appears that they did not believe, for what it says afterward: \"Speak to the children of Israel and take from them a staff, a staff for each… and the man whom I shall choose, his staff shall blossom, and I shall cause to cease from Me\" (verses 17–20) — proof that the people did not believe from this burning that the Levites were chosen and the firstborn were replaced by them; rather, they thought that Moses and Aaron caused the burning, or that the punishment was on account of unauthorized fire which He had not commanded them, and Aaron's incense was the morning incense, as I explained (Leviticus 10:2). And their complaint was only about the burning, not about the swallowing, for HaShem said to Moses, \"Get up from around…\" and the like, and this alludes to the opening of the earth's mouth, and Moses told this to Israel in the name of HaShem. And Dathan and Abiram were more culpable, for they taunted the angels of Elohim, despised His words, and mocked the prophet. And the correct view in my eyes is that the people now believed in the priesthood of Aaron, since fire had already gone forth from before HaShem and consumed his offerings, but they desired that the firstborn be the ministers of the Tabernacle in place of the Levites, and they did not accept the exchange that had been made upon them, for they wanted all the tribes to have a share in the service of the House of HaShem. And so they complained: \"You have killed them\" — for you gave this counsel that they should offer incense like priests, when they were fit for Levitical service, not to be like priests who offer incense. And this is the meaning of \"the staff of Aaron for the house of Levi blossomed\" (Numbers 17:23)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:37.002153254Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}